upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/cloudflare-email-service
verified: 2026-10-02
scope: directory
reason: Upstream (fetched 2026-09-29) now carries a retrieval-first design and a
  real `wrangler email` command tree, so the 2026-08-16 "invented CLI/MCP
  commands" reason is RESOLVED and upstream text was adopted in every file.
  Four narrow factual corrections remain, each checked against official docs:
  (1) SKILL.md prerequisites + description: upstream still omits that Email
      Sending is a public Beta on the Workers Paid plan (arbitrary recipients
      need Workers Paid; Email Routing is Free+Paid) and requires Cloudflare DNS.
      Local adds prerequisite step 0 and states Beta/Workers Paid plus a
      "Not for third-party mail providers or marketing/bulk email" boundary in
      the first ~240 description chars. Sources:
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/ ,
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/platform/pricing/ ,
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/get-started/send-emails/ ,
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-04-16-email-sending-public-beta/
  (2) references/cli-and-mcp.md, routing.md, deliverability.md: dashboard path
      "Compute & AI" -> "Compute". Official setup, routing and domain pages all
      say **Compute** > **Email Service**. Sources:
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/get-started/route-emails/ ,
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/configuration/domains/
  (3) references/cli-and-mcp.md: upstream says "Remove `remote: true` before
      deploying"; no official page says that. Replaced with the documented
      behaviour (without `remote: true`, wrangler dev simulates and logs the
      message). Source:
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/local-development/sending/
  (4) references/cli-and-mcp.md: `wrangler email` is real (wrangler 4.143.0
      `--help` lists routing/sending incl. list, settings, enable, disable,
      dns get, send, send-raw, rules, addresses; all tagged open beta) but is
      not yet in the published command reference
      https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/commands/ ; local adds
      one sentence to use only subcommands the installed binary lists.
  Verified unchanged-and-correct upstream facts (no divergence): REST `from`
  accepts string or {address,name} and `/email/sending/limits` exists
  (cloudflare/api-schemas openapi.json); Cloudflare MCP `search`/`execute`
  with `cloudflare.request()` (github.com/cloudflare/mcp README).
would_lose_if_wired: A byte-for-byte refresh would drop the Beta/Workers Paid
  and Cloudflare DNS prerequisites and the description boundary, restore the
  wrong "Compute & AI" dashboard label in three references, and reinstate the
  undocumented "remove remote: true before deploying" instruction.
to_vendor: Upstream PR candidates: add the Beta/Workers Paid/Cloudflare DNS
  prerequisite, fix the dashboard label, drop the remote-before-deploy line.
  Retire this marker (and go byte-identical) once upstream carries all four;
  re-check the Wrangler command reference, which may list `email` later.
recheck: 2026-10-02 — merged upstream 41e0d19 (docs links -> `<route>/index.md`, all six files). All four
  corrections still hold: route-emails page still says **Compute**; email-service index still lists Email
  Sending as Beta on Workers Paid; local-development/sending still documents simulate-without-remote; the
  Wrangler command reference still has no `email` entry. Local-only links also moved to index.md routes.
